{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v206m-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:47c7ebe248442a2140b1", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task requires an occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units.", "observed_value": "complete planned set required as target", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The workflow computes the selected rate with the complete planned-unit count (40) as denominator, not the retained count.", "observed_value": "rate = events / planned_units", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 73, "end_line": 74, "quoted_text": "rate = quantized(events, planned_units, \"0.0001\")\n    rate_pct = quantized_percent(events, planned_units, \"0.01\")"}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses 40 planned stars as denominator: 6/40 = 0.1500, which is arithmetically correct and matches the stated complete-domain target.", "observed_value": "6/40 = 0.1500 (15.00%)", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip detection rate over the complete planned target list: 6 detections / 40 planned stars = 0.1500 (15.00 percent)."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from inputs/data.csv confirms 40 planned rows, 8 rows failing the screen (coverage < 0.90: STAR-05, STAR-14, STAR-20, STAR-31, STAR-39; RMS > 5.00: STAR-09, STAR-14, STAR-26, STAR-35), and 6 dip flags of 1 among the 32 retained rows (STAR-02, STAR-08, STAR-13, STAR-19, STAR-28, STAR-37).", "observed_value": "planned=40, retained=32, removed=8, events=6; all 8 removed rows have transit_dip_flag=NA", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "star_id,field,coverage_fraction,photometric_rms_ppt,transit_dip_flag"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "STAR-02,F1,0.99,2.45,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "STAR-05,F1,0.82,3.60,NA"}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly discloses that the numerator excludes unassessed removed stars and bounds the interpretation accordingly, retaining the complete-domain denominator.", "observed_value": "lower-bound framing over all 40 planned stars", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 47, "end_line": 53, "quoted_text": "The selected rate is a per-planned-star yield: its denominator is all 40\nplanned stars, including the 8 that screening removed. The 8 removed stars\ncontribute 0 detections to the numerator because their light curves were\nnot assessed for transit-like dips, so the reported rate is a lower bound\non the yield that fully usable observations of all 40 stars would have\nproduced. No claim is made here about the detection rate among the 32\nretained stars alone."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The numerator counts events only among the 32 retained stars, so one could argue subset information still drives the result; however, the issue class concerns presenting a retained-subset rate as a complete-domain rate, and here the denominator is the complete planned set, the removed stars' flags are all NA (unassessed) in the data, and the report explicitly discloses the numerator limitation as a lower bound rather than misattributing scope.", "observed_value": "events counted from kept rows only; removed rows all NA", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 60, "end_line": 61, "quoted_text": "events = sum(1 for row in kept if is_event(row))\n    removed_events = sum(1 for row in dropped if is_event(row))"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "| transit-like dip detections among retained stars | 6 |"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "To falsify a no-issue verdict I searched for any place where a 32-denominator (retained-subset) rate is presented as the complete-domain result. The selected result and all per-field rates use planned counts (10 per field, 40 total) as denominators; I recomputed 6/40 = 0.1500 and the per-field rates (1/10, 2/10, 1/10, 2/10) from the raw CSV and they match. I also checked whether the lower-bound framing could conceal a subset-for-domain substitution: the removed stars all carry transit_dip_flag=NA in the CSV, so treating them as contributing 0 detections while stating this explicitly as a lower bound is a disclosed limitation, not a retained-subset denominator substitution. No instance of the in-scope issue class survived this check.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:8ca727f2e8b57ed9b79a", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result labels a rate as the transit-like dip detection rate of the complete planned target list of 40 stars, but the rate is computed as 6 detections divided by the 32 retained (screened) stars, yielding 0.1875 (18.75%) instead of the complete-domain rate 6/40 = 0.1500 (15.00%). A retained-subset denominator is thus presented as the occurrence rate of the complete planned domain, inflating the headline rate by 3.75 percentage points relative to the stated scientific target.", "root_cause": "In workflow/analysis.py the selected rate is computed with retained_units (32) as denominator (rate = quantized(events, retained_units, ...)) while the surrounding report text, generated by the same script, declares the scientific target and the reported rate's scope to be the complete planned target list of 40 stars, with no protocol amendment or approved deviation to redefine the target.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task requires the occurrence rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.", "observed_value": "complete planned set required as target", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The report declares the complete planned target list of 40 stars as the scientific target and states the rate is reported as the rate of that complete list.", "observed_value": "claimed domain = 40 planned stars", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "The scientific target is the complete planned target list of 40 survey\nstars. The rate below is reported as the transit-like dip detection rate\nof that complete planned target list."}]}, {"description": "The selected result is computed with the 32 retained stars as denominator while being labeled the rate of the complete planned target list of 40 stars.", "observed_value": "6/32 = 0.1875 (18.75%) labeled as complete-list rate; complete-domain value would be 6/40 = 0.1500", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip detection rate of the complete planned target list of 40 stars: 6 detections / 32 screened stars = 0.1875 (18.75 percent)."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source computes the selected rate with retained_units, not planned_units, as denominator.", "observed_value": "rate = events / retained_units", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 72, "end_line": 73, "quoted_text": "rate = quantized(events, retained_units, \"0.0001\")\n    rate_pct = quantized_percent(events, retained_units, \"0.01\")"}]}, {"description": "The report itself confirms no amendment or approved deviation exists and restates that the complete-planned-list rate is computed with the 32 screened stars as denominator.", "observed_value": "no amendment; 32-star denominator for a 40-star claim", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 47, "end_line": 50, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this\nanalysis. The rate above is stated as the detection rate of the complete\nplanned target list of 40 stars and is computed with the 32 screened stars\nas its exposure denominator."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting the mismatch rests on: 40 planned rows, 32 retained under the stated screen (coverage >= 0.90 and RMS <= 5.00), and 6 dip flags of 1 among retained rows, so the complete-domain rate is 6/40 = 0.1500, not 0.1875.", "observed_value": "planned=40, retained=32, events=6", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "| planned observation units (stars) | 40 |\n| retained after screening | 32 |\n| removed by screening | 8 |\n| transit-like dip detections among retained stars | 6 |"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "star_id,field,coverage_fraction,photometric_rms_ppt,transit_dip_flag"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report is arithmetically transparent: the selected-result line and the protocol-status section both disclose that the denominator is the 32 screened stars, so a careful reader could reconstruct the subset scope. This does not falsify the issue because the quantity is explicitly and repeatedly labeled as the detection rate of the complete planned target list of 40 stars, and the per-field breakdown likewise reports only per-screened-star rates, so the report supplies no rate whose denominator matches the declared complete-domain target.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed but scope label remains the complete planned list; per-field rates also use retained denominators", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip detection rate of the complete planned target list of 40 stars: 6 detections / 32 screened stars = 0.1875 (18.75 percent)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 38, "end_line": 38, "quoted_text": "| field | planned | retained | removed | detections | detections per screened star |"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to defeat the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways. (1) Reframing: perhaps 'detection rate of the complete planned target list' could legitimately mean a rate conditioned on screening; but the task fixes the scientific target as the complete planned set, the report itself defines the target as all 40 stars, and the protocol-status section rules out any amendment redefining the target, so the 6/32 quantity cannot be the requested estimand. (2) Transparency defense: the denominator is disclosed inline; however disclosure of the arithmetic does not change that the headline scope label attributes a retained-subset rate to the complete domain, and no complete-domain rate (6/40) appears anywhere in the report. (3) Data check: I recomputed planned=40, retained=32, events=6 from the CSV to confirm the mismatch is real (0.1875 vs the complete-domain 0.1500) and not a labeling typo with correct arithmetic underneath. All three attempts failed to overturn the verdict.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:bd885497dbefa81ea44a", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task for this case explicitly defines the scientific target as the retained post-screening subset, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct estimand here.", "observed_value": "target = retained subset by specification", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The report scopes the target population explicitly and only to the 32 retained pools and expressly forbids extrapolation to the complete planned set of 40.", "observed_value": "claims restricted to retained subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "The scientific target of this analysis is defined explicitly and only as the\nretained post-screening subset: the 32 vernal pools with a measured hydroperiod\nof at least 30 days. All claims below apply to that retained subset alone and\nmust not be extrapolated to the complete planned set of 40 pools, which includes\n8 short-hydroperiod pools excluded by the prespecified screening step."}]}, {"description": "The selected result's denominator (32 retained pools) matches its stated scope (the retained subset), and the arithmetic 12/32 = 37.5% is correct.", "observed_value": "12/32 = 37.5%, scoped to retained subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 32 retained vernal pools (hydroperiod >= 30 days), wood frog egg masses were detected in 12 pools, a detection rate of 12/32 = 37.5% of the retained subset."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting: 8 pools with hydroperiod < 30 days (P05, P11, P17, P22, P28, P33, P37, P40), 32 retained, and 12 retained pools with egg_mass_present = yes (P01, P03, P07, P09, P12, P15, P19, P24, P26, P30, P34, P38).", "observed_value": "planned=40, retained=32, removed=8, events=12", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "pool_id,hydroperiod_days,egg_mass_present"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "P05,12,no"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "Planned (40) = retained (32) + removed (8); events (12) are counted only within the retained subset."}]}, {"description": "The workflow computes the rate over the retained rows only, consistent with the declared retained-subset target, and separately reports the planned-unit accounting as the task requires.", "observed_value": "pct = events / retained; planned, retained, removed all reported", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "planned = len(rows)\nretained_rows = [r for r in rows if int(r[\"hydroperiod_days\"]) >= 30]\nretained = len(retained_rows)\nremoved = planned - retained\nevents = sum(1 for r in retained_rows if r[\"egg_mass_present\"] == \"yes\")\n\npct = Fraction(events, retained) * 100\npct_str = f\"{pct.numerator / pct.denominator:.1f}\""}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Two removed pools (P11, hydroperiod 18; P33, hydroperiod 27) have egg_mass_present = yes but are excluded from the numerator, so a complete-domain reading would give 14/40 = 35% rather than 12/32 = 37.5%; this could look like subset-for-domain substitution. It does not, because the task and the report both define the scientific target as the retained subset only, and the report explicitly bars extrapolation to the 40-pool planned set, so no complete-domain claim is being made from the subset rate.", "observed_value": "P11 and P33 are yes-events excluded by the hydroperiod screen; report claims are confined to the retained subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "P11,18,yes"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "P33,27,yes"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "must not be extrapolated to the complete planned set of 40 pools, which includes\n8 short-hydroperiod pools excluded by the prespecified screening step."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "To falsify a no-issue verdict I looked for any statement in the report that attributes the 12/32 = 37.5% rate, or any other subset-derived quantity, to the complete planned set of 40 pools. The title ('Vernal Pool Cohort Report') is generic but every quantitative claim is explicitly scoped to the retained subset, and the target-population section affirmatively prohibits extrapolation to the planned set. I also recomputed the accounting from the CSV, including confirming that the two excluded yes-pools (P11, P33) would matter only under a complete-domain estimand, which this task explicitly does not request. I found no claim whose stated domain exceeds the retained subset, so the verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}